---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Refund Policy | Where Horses Run"
  description="Refund policy for optional tips made to Where Horses Run."
>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <p class="hero__eyebrow">Payments</p>
    <h1 id="page-title">Refund Policy</h1>
    <p class="hero__summary">This policy applies if optional tip payments are enabled in the future. Payment processing is not currently enabled.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section-grid" aria-label="Refund policy">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Voluntary tips</h2>
      <p>Tips are voluntary payments made for information and content that Where Horses Run has already provided free of charge. A tip does not purchase physical goods, paid membership, betting services, predictions, or entitlement to future content.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Ordinary refund or cancellation requests</h2>
      <p>A correctly processed tip is a voluntary payment for content already provided, so cancellation or a refund after payment is not automatically guaranteed. If you would like a refund, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page. We will review the circumstances and handle the request in accordance with applicable law and the payment processor's rules.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Duplicate, incorrect, or defective payment processing</h2>
      <p>If we confirm a duplicate payment, an unintended payment amount, or another technical payment-processing error, we will refund the affected payment or the amount processed in error.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Unrecognized payments</h2>
      <p>If you do not recognize a payment, do not send card numbers or authentication information. Contact us promptly through the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page so the payment can be investigated and any relevant payment-processor procedure can be explained.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Refund method</h2>
      <p>Approved refunds are normally returned to the original payment method. The time before a refund appears can vary by payment provider and financial institution.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
